{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.q_gl_obstruction_calc","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.q_gl_obstruction_calc","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QGeometricLanglands"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_gl_obstruction_calc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_gl_obstruction_calc","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/q_gl_obstruction_calc.lean#L107-L159","doc":"**Obstruction to q-flatness** (`prop:q-gl-obstruction-calc`).\n\nLet $(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)$ be a quantum observable universe with\n$\\chi(A) \\neq 0$ and obstruction class\n$\\kappa_0 = e(\\xi) \\in H^2(\\mathcal{S}, \\mathbb{G}_m)$.  Then:\n\n1. the intrinsic q-curvature `F^{intr}_q = HKR⁻¹(κ₀)` is nonzero\n   whenever `κ₀ ≠ 0` — **assumed**, as `ctx.intrinsic_curvature_nonzero`\n   (geometric, manuscript);\n2. `∇_q` is q-flat iff its connection-dependent curvature vanishes —\n   **assumed**, as `ctx.q_flatness_equiv` (geometric, manuscript);\n3. at Kummer level `n ≥ 1`, `κ₀ mod n = 0` iff `n ∣ χ(A)` — **derived**\n   by composing the geometric bridge to `χ(A) mod n` (the explicit\n   conditional-class hypothesis `kappa_kummer_bridge`) with the **proved**\n   arithmetic half `kummer_divisibility_criterion`;\n4. for `χ(A) ≠ 0` the obstruction persists at arbitrarily large Kummer\n   levels — **proved** from `obstruction_cofinite_persistence` + (3). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-gl-obstruction-calc","label":"prop:q-gl-obstruction-calc","md":"quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/q-gl-obstruction-calc.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.q_flatness_equiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.q_flatness_equiv","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/q_gl_obstruction_calc.lean#L105-L105","doc":"External theorem / missing input: q-flatness is equivalent to vanishing connection-dependent curvature ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.intrinsic_curvature_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.intrinsic_curvature_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/q_gl_obstruction_calc.lean#L103-L103","doc":"External theorem / missing input: intrinsic curvature is nonzero when κ₀ ≠ 0 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.kappa_kummer_bridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.kappa_kummer_bridge","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/q_gl_obstruction_calc.lean#L100-L100","doc":"**Geometric Kummer bridge** (class-axiomatised geometric input, per\nAGENTS.md §3b-cond). At Kummer level `n ≥ 1`, the mod-`n` reduction of\nthe obstruction class `κ₀ ∈ H²(𝒮, 𝔾_m)` — the connecting map of the\nKummer exact sequence `0 → μ_n → 𝔾_m --(·)ⁿ--> 𝔾_m → 0` in sheaf\ncohomology — vanishes iff the Euler characteristic satisfies\n`χ(A) ≡ 0 (mod n)`.  This is the genuinely *geometric* half of part 3:\nit computes `κ₀ mod n` by `χ(A) mod n` (the Yekutieli central-extension\ncomputation `H²(𝒮, 𝔾_m) ≅ ℤ` with `κ₀ ↔ χ(A)`), a fact not derivable\nfrom Mathlib.  It is an **input** to the theorem — *not* part 3's\nconclusion (`κ₀ mod n = 0 ↔ n ∣ χ(A)`), which is *derived* by composing\nthis bridge with the proved arithmetic\n`QGeometricLanglands.kummer_divisibility_criterion`.  Encoding it as a\nnamed field (rather than an internal `sorry`) makes the conditional\ndependency explicit in the theorem's signature and auditable from the\ncontext. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.kappa_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.kappa_zero","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/q_gl_obstruction_calc.lean#L83-L83","doc":"Predicate: the obstruction class `κ₀ = e(ξ) ∈ H²(𝒮, 𝔾_m)` vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.kappa_vanishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.kappa_vanishes","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/q_gl_obstruction_calc.lean#L81-L81","doc":"Predicate: `κ_0 mod n` vanishes at Kummer level `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.R_connection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.R_connection","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/q_gl_obstruction_calc.lean#L79-L79","doc":"The connection-dependent curvature `R(∇)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.q_flat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.q_flat","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/q_gl_obstruction_calc.lean#L77-L77","doc":"Predicate: `∇_q` is q-flat. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.F_intr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.F_intr","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/q_gl_obstruction_calc.lean#L75-L75","doc":"Intrinsic q-curvature `F^{intr}_q` of a q-flat connection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.chi_A_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.chi_A_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/q_gl_obstruction_calc.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.chi_A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.chi_A","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/q_gl_obstruction_calc.lean#L72-L72","doc":"Euler characteristic `χ(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.CategoricalObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.CategoricalObj","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/q_gl_obstruction_calc.lean#L70-L70","doc":"The categorical object / monoidal structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/q_gl_obstruction_calc.lean#L68-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGlObstructionCalcContext","kind":"class","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/q_gl_obstruction_calc.lean#L65-L105","doc":"Abstract context for the `q_gl_obstruction_calc` claim — manuscript-themed\ntyped fields standing in for the geometric objects of\n`prop:q-gl-obstruction-calc`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}